iation with government expenditure in the Keynesian framework. Additionally, the lowercase \"g\" in GLMs highlights the importance of link functions in modeling relationships between predictors and response variables. Understanding these various dimensions of \"G\" is essential for econometric analysis, as it informs model specification, interpretation of results, and the application of economic theory in empirical research."], "parameters": {"model": "nomic-embed-text"}}, "key": "embeddings_320159d48d95298fb310cc41e6264ec1361a0fd38fd09fe703235b933d8d194f_v2"}